{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1322407-thin-blood-alchemy-counterfeit-duration","id":1322407,"title":"Thin-Blood Alchemy Counterfeit duration","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-07-05T06:50:30-07:00","id":1322407,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon5.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Thin-Blood Alchemy Counterfeit duration","content":"Hello!<br /> <br /> I play a thin-blooded alchemist (fixatio method), and I am both intrigued and confused about the Alchemy's description in VtM5 core rulebook. I can't find references about how long is the duration of the formulas. For example, I create a counterfeit Presense level 1 potion, which grants me an ability to duplicate Awe power. Or second, which makes my senses Hightened, as per 1st level power of Auspex. How long I can use it? One roll? One scene? One night? The whole story? I can imagine arguments for all of the options (except first one, it's obviously not 1 roll), but I'm interested, what was intended by game designers.<br /> <br /> Does anyone know? I don't really want to trigger a speculation fest, 'cause I can think out a solution by myself, but if I missed something, let me know, please.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11161-leeder","name":"Leeder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11161_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-06T08:50:29-07:00","id":1322600,"title":"","content":"The duration of the power. Just that. If its a turn, a turn, if its a scene a scene. What i do not know if its passive what happens, but i would roll it one night.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25214-sharei","name":"Sharei","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-06T12:15:08-07:00","id":1322626,"title":"","content":"I would have said passive powers last the scene, but lasting the night is also a valid ruling.<br /> <br /> But yes. You get one &quot;use&quot; of the power. If it's a power that's activated and takes effect immediately, like most of Dominate, once it's used it's gone. If the effects stick around for a while, like with Protean, it lasts the normal power duration. If it lasts indefinitely (a &quot;passive&quot; effect), it's up to the ST, since the rules don't say.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-07T23:35:45-07:00","id":1322896,"title":"","content":"Could you please show me what makes you think it is for one use of power? Because for me it looks slightly silly, noting how many bottles an alchemist is allowed to carry and how long and difficult it takes to brew one. And I don't see any preconditions of that point of view in the discipline or in the concept of alchemy in general.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11161,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11161-leeder","user":"Leeder","date":". 07-08-2019, 02:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11161-leeder","name":"Leeder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11161_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-29T13:08:29-07:00","id":1399900,"title":"","content":"Might I revive this thread by any chance? I didn't want to spam the board with new threads for short questions.<br /> <br /> I know that the rules for Blood Alchemy are very thin (pun intended) and that the golden rules says &quot;Do whatever works for your group.&quot;.<br /> But as far as I thought Blood Alchemy (for example 'Far Reach') in the fixatio method would work this way:<ul><li>1. Drink the 'potion'.</li> <li>2. One telekinetic action.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> (If you want a second one<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><ul><li>3. Drink another, different and separately prepared potion.</li> <li>4. Telekinetic action.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> As I recently got into LA By Night I saw the following in Season One:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">One of the Thin Bloods used Far Reach for one action and afterwards tried to use it again on Victor, to disarm him.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> As LA By Night seems to be considered canon, I'm wondering if I got it wrong. Are one-action disciplines are supposed to work more often? If yes: How often? A scene?<br /> <br /> I'd really appreciate the help and feedback.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">&quot;Life's barely long enough to get good at one thing. So be careful what you get good at.&quot;</span></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26196-saturno","name":"Saturno","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26196_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}